     "prompt_group": "tr:p030",
     "text": "Her mind is not a lantern in the skull but a tide moving through eight hinged constellations; each arm tastes the dark, argues in suction cups, remembers stones by their bruises, and solves the crevice before any center agrees to name it. Thought ripples outward, blue with copper blood, while skin e"
    }
   ]
